                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Do consumers pay more for sustainable products?</h3>
                                        <p>Yes — 5-10% premium in India, 15-30% in USA / UK / Australia. Requires credibility (certification, data).</p>
                                        <h3>Is B Corp certification worth the cost?</h3>
                                        <p>For most premium brands, yes. Timeline 6-14 months, cost $3K-40K. Lifts CVR 5-12% in receptive markets.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest sustainability marketing mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Leading with vague virtue claims. Consumers reward specific data ('X kg CO2 saved') and punish generic 'we care' copy.</p>
                                        <h3>Should sustainability be the main brand pitch?</h3>
                                        <p>No — lead with product benefit; sustainability is a differentiator. Sustainability-only positioning underperforms in most markets.</p>
